WEBVTT

00:03.000 --> 00:05.843
(Western drama theme playing)

00:37.982 --> 00:39.152
(music stops)
Ow!

00:39.203 --> 00:41.108
There's a rock right there!

00:41.174 --> 00:43.103
There's a huge rock right there,

00:43.104 --> 00:44.173
and it's covered up by grass

00:44.241 --> 00:45.830
and there's no way
you can see it.

00:45.898 --> 00:47.302
And I got lucky.

00:47.368 --> 00:49.022
But someone else could
hurt themselves,

00:49.091 --> 00:52.286
and, and a small cut is a, is a
death sentence in these times,

00:52.351 --> 00:54.291
so let's just, you know,
let's...

00:54.358 --> 00:56.900
let's get these rocks out
of here.

00:56.968 --> 00:58.805
(show theme resumes)

01:16.717 --> 01:19.591
♪ There's a fuzzy bunny
rabbit on the train ♪

01:19.659 --> 01:22.133
♪ There's a fuzzy bunny rabbit
on the train ♪

01:22.202 --> 01:24.677
♪ And he's wiggling his nose
and his little bunny ts ♪

01:24.745 --> 01:27.433
♪ There's a fuzzy bunny rabbit
on the train. ♪

01:27.502 --> 01:29.542
Okay, what else we got
on that train?

01:29.610 --> 01:31.229
A kitty cat.
A doggy.

01:31.298 --> 01:33.405
Kevin Smith 'cause he's too fat
to ride a plane!

01:33.474 --> 01:35.076
Okay, I heard kitty cat.

01:35.144 --> 01:38.355
♪ Oh... there's a kitty cat
a-riding on the train ♪

01:38.424 --> 01:39.793
God, you know,
I don't know why

01:39.859 --> 01:41.598
this guy's wife isn't here
watching this stuff.

01:41.665 --> 01:43.637
If I were her,
I'd be here every show.

01:43.705 --> 01:45.846
♪ There's a kitty cat
a-riding on the train. ♪

01:45.932 --> 01:49.359
Thanks, everybody.
See you next week.

01:49.443 --> 01:50.947
Yay! He's a good singer.

01:51.014 --> 01:52.550
Yeah, I've been catching
his library shows

01:52.618 --> 01:54.693
since there were only, like,
three or four kids here.

01:54.761 --> 01:56.145
You should have
been here, man.

01:56.213 --> 01:57.382
<i>Those were the shows.</i>

01:57.450 --> 01:59.541
Oh, looks like
somebody made a friend.

01:59.609 --> 02:01.479
I know.
Aren't they cute together?

02:01.548 --> 02:03.738
Adorable. I'm Lois.

02:03.823 --> 02:05.192
Hi, I'm Hope.

02:05.260 --> 02:08.003
Any relation
to Bob Hope? (laughs)

02:08.054 --> 02:09.206
I'm kidding!

02:09.257 --> 02:10.461
I'm kind of known
for having

02:10.529 --> 02:11.866
a twisted sense
of humor.

02:11.933 --> 02:13.770
<i>Oh, don't worry,
I watch Regis and Kelly.</i>

02:13.838 --> 02:15.059
I can handle it.

02:15.127 --> 02:16.697
Oh, so, you know.

02:16.765 --> 02:18.405
This is my husband Ben.

02:18.457 --> 02:19.659
Hi, glad to know you.

02:19.727 --> 02:21.496
Gosh, you know,
our little Scotty seems

02:21.565 --> 02:23.955
to be having such a good time
with your son.

02:24.023 --> 02:25.277
Would you be interested

02:25.344 --> 02:27.000
in getting them together
for a playdate?

02:27.068 --> 02:29.675
Oh, that sounds
like a wonderful idea.

02:29.743 --> 02:31.178
Look at them.
They're getting along

02:31.247 --> 02:33.220
like Billy Bob Thornton
and his cat.

02:33.288 --> 02:35.092
WOMAN:
Billy Bob?

02:35.159 --> 02:36.866
Leave me alone!
I'm taking a bath!

02:40.729 --> 02:42.267
Stewie, do you want
to be the Autobots

02:42.333 --> 02:43.771
or the Decepticons?

02:43.839 --> 02:45.476
What's with all
these labels, man?

02:45.544 --> 02:47.852
Autobots, Decepticons,
gay, straight--

02:47.920 --> 02:49.889
just pick a few robots,
and let's party.

02:49.976 --> 02:51.547
Hey, what's
going on in here?

02:51.615 --> 02:53.303
Oh, hello, Brian.
We're playing Transformers.

02:53.371 --> 02:55.074
Oh, cool.
Who's this little guy?

02:55.159 --> 02:57.099
It's my new friend, Scotty.

02:57.169 --> 02:58.504
Do you mind? We're busy.
Oh.

02:58.570 --> 03:00.141
Hi, doggie.
You want to play with us?

03:00.209 --> 03:01.413
Scotty, Scotty, it's fine.
It's fine.

03:01.481 --> 03:02.617
You don't have to.

03:02.684 --> 03:03.686
He doesn't know
Transformers.

03:03.754 --> 03:04.958
Yeah, actually,
I-I'd love to play.

03:05.026 --> 03:06.128
Wh-Who should I be?

03:06.197 --> 03:07.784
Should I be one
of these guys?

03:07.868 --> 03:09.840
I-I'll be this guy.
Who's this guy, huh?

03:09.907 --> 03:10.979
What's this guy's story?

03:11.045 --> 03:12.332
That's Optimus Prime.

03:12.399 --> 03:13.937
You can't be him.
Scotty's Optimus Prime.

03:14.006 --> 03:16.513
Oh, all right. Well, I'll be,
I'll be this guy.

03:16.581 --> 03:17.951
How about this guy?
(growls)

03:18.019 --> 03:20.258
What was that?
Did you just growl?

03:20.326 --> 03:22.700
What robot growls?
That's Starscream.

03:22.769 --> 03:24.238
He's a Decepticon.
I'm the Decepticons.

03:24.307 --> 03:25.880
Look, why don't you
just beat it?

03:25.948 --> 03:27.483
All right,
all right, relax.

03:27.550 --> 03:29.625
I'll-I'll just, I'll be
this guy over here.

03:29.693 --> 03:31.697
That's He-Man.
We're playing Transformers.

03:31.765 --> 03:34.139
Well, maybe this is the one
where He-Man visits.

03:34.206 --> 03:36.563
Brian, how is He-Man
supposed to get to Cybertron?

03:36.631 --> 03:37.901
Hey, "Up, up,
and away," right?

03:37.969 --> 03:39.171
He-Man doesn't fly.

03:39.239 --> 03:41.178
Look, why are you being
such a dick about this?

03:41.246 --> 03:42.616
I'm just trying
to join in.

03:42.684 --> 03:44.523
Yeah, you don't know what
you're talking about, okay?

03:44.591 --> 03:45.710
You sound like...
That's not fair.

03:45.778 --> 03:47.099
I think I'm doing
pretty well.

03:47.167 --> 03:48.618
No, you don't know
the characters, Brian.

03:48.687 --> 03:49.788
You don't know
the characters.

03:49.856 --> 03:51.196
If you could hear
yourself right now,

03:51.263 --> 03:52.364
you would not stop
throwing up.

03:52.433 --> 03:53.634
You can't just put He-Man

03:53.703 --> 03:54.807
in Transformers'
world, all right?

03:54.875 --> 03:57.081
He wouldn't be able
to get to Cybertron

03:57.150 --> 03:59.958
because he lives in Eternia,
and Eternia is in

04:00.025 --> 04:01.228
an entirely
different dimension.

04:01.295 --> 04:03.169
He can just take
his rocket ship.

04:03.237 --> 04:06.143
Get... get out of here.

04:10.276 --> 04:13.386
<i>TV ANNOUNCER: We now return to The Post
"Roe vs. Wade"Brady Bunch.</i>

04:13.454 --> 04:15.895
Greg! Marcia! Get down here!

04:15.963 --> 04:17.799
(barking playfully)

04:19.240 --> 04:21.496
Oh, you two are such a handful!

04:21.580 --> 04:23.585
(sitcom transition music plays)

04:28.853 --> 04:30.644
Oh, I'm getting
some steam.

04:30.711 --> 04:32.082
Picking up steam
here, Scotty.

04:32.150 --> 04:33.268
You'd better look out.

04:33.337 --> 04:34.839
I don't feel so well.

04:36.747 --> 04:40.057
Uh, kind of bad timing,
but gin.

04:40.125 --> 04:43.550
Hey, Lois, that
not-Stewie kid fell over!

04:43.601 --> 04:45.476
Oh, my God,
he's unconscious!

04:45.544 --> 04:46.712
Peter, what happened?!

04:46.781 --> 04:48.619
Eh, you know me, Lois,
I don't pry.

04:48.688 --> 04:50.325
Peter, he's not moving!

04:50.393 --> 04:52.031
We gotta get him
to the hospital!

04:52.099 --> 04:54.038
You got it, Lois!
To the Peter-rang!

04:57.083 --> 04:58.619
(laughter fades out)

05:00.896 --> 05:02.631
(laughter fades back in)

05:02.716 --> 05:04.472
(crashing)

05:04.540 --> 05:05.743
Just for the record,

05:05.812 --> 05:07.682
I was at the hospital
for a brief moment.

05:10.960 --> 05:12.464
Mrs. Griffin,
it's a good thing

05:12.531 --> 05:13.803
you brought this child in.

05:13.871 --> 05:15.174
Why? Is he okay?

05:15.242 --> 05:16.478
I'm afraid
he's very sick.

05:16.545 --> 05:18.920
In fact, his lab-work
shows he is suffering

05:18.988 --> 05:20.525
from Hodgkin's lymphoma.

05:20.593 --> 05:22.631
Oh, my God!

05:22.701 --> 05:24.305
Are you saying
Scotty has cancer?!

05:24.373 --> 05:26.344
I don't know, I didn't
read the whole Wikipedia entry,

05:26.411 --> 05:29.154
but the good news is that what
he has is highly treatable

05:29.221 --> 05:30.358
with radiation first,

05:30.425 --> 05:32.064
and if necessary,
chemotherapy.

05:34.907 --> 05:36.611
(coughs,
clears throat)

05:36.679 --> 05:37.949
Oh, for God's sake.

05:38.018 --> 05:39.522
Look, do you have
any idea

05:39.591 --> 05:40.927
how expensive
medical school is?

05:40.992 --> 05:42.229
No, I don't.

05:42.298 --> 05:44.238
Well, it's probably
pretty expensive.

05:44.306 --> 05:46.528
Lois! We came as soon
as we got your call.

05:46.596 --> 05:48.168
Oh, Hope, Ben,

05:48.235 --> 05:50.777
I'm so sorry to have
to tell you this,

05:50.845 --> 05:52.481
but Scotty has...

05:52.549 --> 05:53.852
Cancer. We know.

05:53.921 --> 05:54.889
You do?

05:54.957 --> 05:56.359
Yes, we're aware
of his condition.

05:56.428 --> 05:58.500
But you shouldn't have
brought him to the hospital

05:58.568 --> 06:00.105
without talking to us first.

06:00.174 --> 06:02.313
Why wouldn't we bring him?
He was unconscious.

06:02.381 --> 06:04.087
He clearly
needed treatment.

06:04.155 --> 06:06.493
Oh, no, he doesn't
receive treatment.

06:06.561 --> 06:07.432
What?!

06:07.499 --> 06:09.606
We're Christian Scientists.

06:09.671 --> 06:11.343
We don't accept medical care
for ourselves,

06:11.411 --> 06:13.117
and we don't permit it
for our children.

06:13.185 --> 06:14.420
But your son
has cancer!

06:14.488 --> 06:15.877
Wait a minute.
Christian Science.

06:15.943 --> 06:17.414
Is that, is that
that thing

06:17.481 --> 06:18.886
all them gaybo
Hollywood actors do

06:18.954 --> 06:21.444
to keep their stuff away
from other guys' butts?

06:21.512 --> 06:23.584
Don't you understand?
Scotty needs help.

06:23.652 --> 06:25.391
And he'll get it...
through faith.

06:25.459 --> 06:26.561
That's right.

06:26.629 --> 06:28.902
We will heal him
with the power of prayer.

06:30.509 --> 06:32.967
Y-You can't just let them
just walk out of here!

06:33.052 --> 06:34.505
Oh, I think
they'll be back.

06:34.573 --> 06:36.511
Are those their keys?
No, they're my keys.

06:41.104 --> 06:42.708
And they said because
of their faith,

06:42.725 --> 06:44.229
they don't believe
in medicine.

06:44.297 --> 06:46.738
Mom, I think there's a lot
of religions that do that.

06:46.806 --> 06:49.581
Well, that may be, Meg, but that
poor little baby has cancer,

06:49.647 --> 06:51.855
and they're just gonna take him
home and pray over him?!

06:51.923 --> 06:53.226
Well, that's what they do.

06:53.295 --> 06:54.931
They believe that disease
is just an illusion.

06:54.999 --> 06:57.775
And the only way to fight it
is to make your faith stronger.

06:57.843 --> 07:00.349
Illusions?! You want to
talk about illusions?!

07:00.417 --> 07:02.556
If you die tomorrow,

07:02.625 --> 07:04.745
you think we're gonna be devastated!
But you know what?!

07:04.814 --> 07:06.989
We're just gonna go out
and buy another dog!

07:07.057 --> 07:08.928
<i>And maybe this dog
will fetch a stick</i>

07:08.995 --> 07:11.068
and bring me my slippers
instead of prattling on

07:11.136 --> 07:13.109
about the pros and cons
of various religions!

07:13.176 --> 07:15.182
Chris, I think you've had
too much sugar cereal.

07:15.250 --> 07:17.355
I think I haven't had enough!

07:18.827 --> 07:20.967
Peter, I have to go talk
to the Jennings

07:21.034 --> 07:23.928
and ask them to reconsider
getting treatment for Scotty.

07:23.995 --> 07:25.232
I'm going with
you, Lois.

07:25.300 --> 07:26.504
Yeah, I'll go, too.

07:26.572 --> 07:28.441
All right, but try
to keep your mouth shut, okay?

07:28.509 --> 07:29.981
You have a habit
of saying the wrong thing.

07:31.186 --> 07:33.326
During his 22-year reign,

07:33.391 --> 07:36.436
this French monarch known
as "The Spider King" had

07:36.504 --> 07:39.746
an ongoing feud with Charles
the Bold, Duke of Burgundy.

07:39.815 --> 07:40.650
Peter?

07:40.720 --> 07:42.355
Who was King Louis XII?

07:42.422 --> 07:46.301
Ooh, I'm sorry, Peter, we were
looking for King Louis XI.

07:46.370 --> 07:48.676
Ah, damn it, I knew that!

07:48.744 --> 07:50.449
Ah, well, (bleep) me
in the (bleep)

07:50.517 --> 07:52.188
with a big,
black (bleep).

07:52.255 --> 07:54.296
King Louis XI.

07:54.363 --> 07:55.533
Tim, select.

07:57.289 --> 07:59.480
(doorbell rings)

08:00.719 --> 08:03.525
Oh, Lois, Peter,
come on in.

08:03.592 --> 08:05.701
We were just praying
for Scotty's recovery.

08:05.768 --> 08:07.471
If you'd like,
you can join us.

08:07.539 --> 08:09.663
Well, that's what we wanted
to talk to you about.

08:09.747 --> 08:11.786
You'd better not just have
church toys.

08:11.854 --> 08:14.580
Look, I don't mean to question
your religious beliefs,

08:14.646 --> 08:16.654
but as a mother,
I just can't bear the thought

08:16.722 --> 08:19.329
of little Scotty
not getting the help he needs.

08:19.396 --> 08:21.034
You really needn't worry, Lois.

08:21.102 --> 08:22.672
Scotty will get all
the help he needs.

08:22.740 --> 08:23.709
From where?

08:23.776 --> 08:25.332
From here.

08:25.401 --> 08:27.405
<i>Science and Health with Key
to the Scriptures</i>

08:27.472 --> 08:29.246
by Mary Baker Eddy?

08:29.314 --> 08:30.382
Let me see that.

08:32.355 --> 08:35.332
This is your god?! A woman?!

08:35.400 --> 08:37.371
Well, she's the founder
of our faith.

08:37.439 --> 08:40.046
Oh, really? So with this book
from the 1800s,

08:40.115 --> 08:43.092
you can pray away paralysis
or terminal illness?

08:43.159 --> 08:45.263
Yes, we would pray for
anyone who's afflicted.

08:45.331 --> 08:47.874
Well, then I'll tell you who you
should really be praying for.

08:47.942 --> 08:48.909
Out-of-work clowns.

08:59.547 --> 09:01.150
I need 40.

09:06.334 --> 09:07.974
Ben, Hope, please,

09:08.042 --> 09:10.916
I just want to do anything
I can to help your son.

09:10.984 --> 09:13.356
Well, you can, Lois.
Stay and pray with us.

09:13.424 --> 09:15.198
I think you'll find
that with God's love

09:15.265 --> 09:16.735
and a true belief,

09:16.803 --> 09:18.775
all manner of miracles
are possible.

09:18.844 --> 09:20.914
Look, I'm a churchgoer, too,

09:20.983 --> 09:23.424
but sometimes prayer
isn't enough.

09:23.493 --> 09:24.863
He needs professional
medical care.

09:24.930 --> 09:26.836
You know, Lois, this couch
would be perfect

09:26.905 --> 09:28.877
for one of your red wine
pass-outs.

09:28.944 --> 09:30.581
Look, we appreciate
your concern, Lois,

09:30.649 --> 09:31.988
but Scotty is our son,

09:32.056 --> 09:34.529
and we have to tend
to him as we see fit.

09:34.594 --> 09:37.539
But your son is sick!
He needs help!

09:37.606 --> 09:39.546
Um, does your god also not
believe in

09:39.611 --> 09:40.864
putting out snacks
for the guests?

09:40.932 --> 09:42.135
Come on, Lois.

09:42.203 --> 09:43.524
I think we're wasting
our time here.

09:43.592 --> 09:45.649
They're obviously very committed
to their beliefs.

09:45.733 --> 09:47.437
But their beliefs
are crazy, Brian.

09:47.505 --> 09:49.445
I don't know
who's crazier--

09:49.513 --> 09:51.468
these people or those
Seventh-Day Adventists.

09:51.535 --> 09:52.605
I'm a Methodist.

09:52.673 --> 09:54.378
We believe that
the Lord is our Savior,

09:54.446 --> 09:56.853
and we remember Him
by going to church

09:56.921 --> 09:58.356
and praising Him
every Sunday.

09:58.424 --> 09:59.693
I'm a Seventh-Day
Adventist.

09:59.762 --> 10:01.803
We believe all the same
things that you believe,

10:01.871 --> 10:03.372
but we go to church
on Saturdays.

10:03.440 --> 10:05.381
What...?!

10:05.466 --> 10:07.269
(laughing crazily)

10:07.337 --> 10:08.641
Ga-ga-ga-ga-gahh!

10:08.692 --> 10:09.695
Whoo-hoo-hoo-hoo!

10:09.779 --> 10:11.719
Hoo-hoo! Hoo-hoo!
Hoo-hoo! Hoo-hoo!

10:14.610 --> 10:16.216
I know it's
frustrating, Lois,

10:16.285 --> 10:18.356
but the fact is,
there are no laws that say

10:18.423 --> 10:20.797
those people have to take
their child to the doctor.

10:20.865 --> 10:22.304
How can that be?

10:22.372 --> 10:24.944
Children are citizens, too.
They should have rights.

10:25.012 --> 10:27.353
Well, it's
a tricky area, Lois.

10:27.421 --> 10:29.762
You could file a suit,
but that could take months,

10:29.829 --> 10:31.401
and even then,
there's no guarantee

10:31.468 --> 10:33.106
the court wouldn't support
the parents' right

10:33.175 --> 10:34.478
to practice their religion.

10:34.544 --> 10:36.618
How could we live in
a country that would allow

10:36.686 --> 10:38.158
a sick child to die?

10:38.225 --> 10:40.848
Look, this country was founded
by people who came here

10:40.915 --> 10:42.386
to escape
religious persecution.

10:42.454 --> 10:44.828
They made sure we all had
a right to religious freedom,

10:44.896 --> 10:46.936
and it's my job
to protect that.

10:47.004 --> 10:48.607
So there's nothing
we can do?

10:48.674 --> 10:52.386
You could contribute
to the Policeman's Ball.

10:52.454 --> 10:53.438
What?!

10:53.463 --> 10:55.450
What does that have
to do with a sick child?

10:55.499 --> 10:57.003
Look, it's
a nice night out,

10:57.068 --> 10:58.439
you're eating
at a fancy buffet,

10:58.507 --> 11:00.314
the captain does
his Al Pacino...

11:00.382 --> 11:02.687
Joe, we're really more
of a Fireman's Ball family.

11:02.755 --> 11:05.531
<i>Oh, yeah? Are the firemen gonna
come and put out the rape?!</i>

11:05.600 --> 11:07.084
(sighs)

11:07.151 --> 11:08.824
Peter, we can't
let this happen.

11:08.892 --> 11:10.430
I-I mean, we're parents.

11:10.498 --> 11:12.302
What if this was
one of our kids?

11:12.370 --> 11:13.858
It's too bad we're
not the A-Team.

11:13.925 --> 11:16.031
'Cause then we could just go
in there and steal that kid.

11:16.099 --> 11:17.770
I don't know
about that, Peter.

11:17.839 --> 11:19.326
Kidnapping is
against the law.

11:19.395 --> 11:21.165
<i>It's too bad we're
not Taken from Taken.</i>

11:21.234 --> 11:23.239
Then I could dip my
head in brown paint

11:23.306 --> 11:25.380
and galumph around Europe
looking for my hot daughter.

11:25.448 --> 11:27.402
Although is it any worse
than what they're doing?

11:27.471 --> 11:29.043
They're letting a kid die.

11:29.111 --> 11:30.346
It's too bad we're
not Dragonheart.

11:30.414 --> 11:32.116
Then we could just fly
around on a dragon

11:32.169 --> 11:33.072
and forget
about all this.

11:33.140 --> 11:34.277
You know what?

11:34.346 --> 11:35.779
That's exactly
what we should do.

11:35.847 --> 11:37.888
What? What the hell are
you talking about?

11:37.956 --> 11:39.760
I'm talking about
us going in there

11:39.828 --> 11:41.869
and taking that kid
and getting him some help.

11:41.937 --> 11:43.406
I mean, I know it's wrong,

11:43.474 --> 11:45.063
but it's better than
just letting him die.

11:45.130 --> 11:46.499
Hey, that's not
a bad idea.

11:46.568 --> 11:48.105
It's like we're doing
a public service.

11:48.174 --> 11:50.480
Like those idiots who get
together to paint a school.

11:50.548 --> 11:53.191
This underachieving,
crime-ridden school

11:53.256 --> 11:55.095
is now fawn beige,

11:55.162 --> 11:58.056
thanks to guilty white people
with no weekend plans!

11:58.124 --> 11:59.961
OTHERS:
Yay!

12:04.177 --> 12:05.829
Peter, what the hell?

12:05.898 --> 12:07.168
Where's your ski mask?

12:07.236 --> 12:08.807
It's kind of hard to
breathe in those things,

12:08.875 --> 12:10.179
so I just dressed up
like Harry Potter.

12:10.247 --> 12:11.181
(sighs)

12:11.250 --> 12:12.418
All right, let's go.

12:12.486 --> 12:14.428
Lois, if anything
should happen to us,

12:14.493 --> 12:17.670
I want you to know, I haven't
been happy for a long time.

12:17.738 --> 12:20.345
Yes, Peter, you've
told me that, like, ten times.

12:24.828 --> 12:26.533
All right,
all the lights are out.

12:26.601 --> 12:27.603
They must be asleep.

12:27.671 --> 12:29.776
It's go time.

12:32.806 --> 12:34.241
Peter, what the
hell was that?

12:34.310 --> 12:35.614
That's what you do, Lois.

12:35.682 --> 12:37.135
Okay, now,
take this walkie-talkie

12:37.202 --> 12:39.109
and confirm that I'm at
the various checkpoints.

12:39.177 --> 12:40.913
Oh. Okay.

12:40.981 --> 12:43.556
"Peter up on a telephone pole"?

12:43.624 --> 12:44.726
Check.

12:44.793 --> 12:47.100
"Peter cutting the wires
to the alarm"?

12:47.170 --> 12:48.038
Check.

12:48.107 --> 12:49.376
"Sexy Peter

12:49.443 --> 12:50.946
distracting the guards"?

12:51.014 --> 12:52.486
Check.

12:52.553 --> 12:54.426
Hello, boys.

12:54.492 --> 12:56.751
Come up and have sex
with me some time.

12:56.836 --> 12:59.557
"Van full of Peters
who all have stern faces

12:59.626 --> 13:01.500
because they're about
to pull off a heist"?

13:01.568 --> 13:03.138
Check.

13:03.204 --> 13:06.332
"Upside-down Peter who isn't
revealed to be upside-down

13:06.399 --> 13:08.840
until the camera spins around
and shows that he is"?

13:10.011 --> 13:11.432
Check.

13:11.501 --> 13:13.839
"Peter in an open airplane door

13:13.907 --> 13:16.818
slapping other Peters on the
back as they parachute out"?

13:16.902 --> 13:19.309
Go, go, go, go, go,
go, go, go, go, go!

13:19.360 --> 13:20.311
Check!

13:20.379 --> 13:22.419
"Super gymnastic Asian Peter

13:22.487 --> 13:25.261
contorted into a box that will
be delivered into the house"?

13:26.501 --> 13:27.803
<i>Hai!</i>

13:27.871 --> 13:29.441
"Peter who hasn't answered

13:29.509 --> 13:31.516
because something has gone
terribly wrong"?

13:31.583 --> 13:33.254
Peter? Peter, are you there?

13:35.847 --> 13:38.122
Now, let's go get that kid.

13:38.187 --> 13:40.228
Okay, he's in the
left upstairs bedroom.

13:40.295 --> 13:42.602
All right, you keep the car
going in case there's trouble.

13:47.486 --> 13:49.641
All right,
I got him, Lois.

13:49.709 --> 13:51.549
(quietly): Peter, what the--
that's not Scotty!

13:51.617 --> 13:52.986
That's Ben!

13:53.055 --> 13:55.496
Oh. Well, you know, we ain't
known this family that long.

13:55.564 --> 13:57.099
I'm still learning
everybody's names.

13:57.167 --> 13:59.674
Damn it, put him back and
go get Scotty, the baby!

13:59.742 --> 14:02.419
Okay, so I'll go get the baby,
and while I'm doing that,

14:02.486 --> 14:05.127
maybe you do something
about that snatchy tone.

14:08.253 --> 14:09.691
Lois, is this the right one?!

14:09.759 --> 14:10.929
Shh! Peter!

14:10.997 --> 14:12.200
Yes. Now, come on.

14:15.346 --> 14:16.281
HOPE:
What was that?

14:16.349 --> 14:17.316
BEN:
I don't know.

14:17.385 --> 14:18.152
It came from
Scotty's room.

14:18.219 --> 14:19.559
(tires screech)

14:21.733 --> 14:23.404
All right, we did it!

14:23.489 --> 14:25.579
Yes! We got the kid
and the treasure.

14:25.661 --> 14:26.800
Peter, there's
no treasure.

14:28.555 --> 14:30.428
Oh, well, never mind, then.

14:36.854 --> 14:38.459
<i>TV ANNOUNCER:
We now return to One-Hour</i>

14:38.484 --> 14:39.997
<i>Crime Show Where the Murderer</i>

14:39.998 --> 14:41.901
<i>is the Most Famous Person
in the Credits.</i>

14:41.969 --> 14:43.607
I think you're gonna want
to take a look at this.

14:43.675 --> 14:44.880
What do we got?

14:44.948 --> 14:46.451
Looks like somebody
had a rough night out.

14:46.519 --> 14:47.871
Boy, you can
say that again.

14:47.924 --> 14:49.229
Better get the
coroner down here.

14:49.296 --> 14:50.965
He's still got his watch
and his wallet.

14:51.049 --> 14:52.337
Guess that rules out robbery.

14:52.406 --> 14:54.278
Stabbed 17 times
in the chest;

14:54.346 --> 14:56.935
I'd say the murderer knew
the victim intimately.

15:00.181 --> 15:02.588
Good evening, I'm Tom Tucker
with some breaking news.

15:02.656 --> 15:05.063
A local kidnapping
has rocked Quahog tonight.

15:05.131 --> 15:06.803
"Rocked Quahog"? Really?

15:06.869 --> 15:08.171
The whole town is r--

15:08.239 --> 15:09.511
The family maybe... is rocked.

15:09.579 --> 15:11.484
But the whole--
All right, well, in any event,

15:11.552 --> 15:14.228
we now go live to Asian reporter
Tricia Takanawa.

15:14.296 --> 15:16.500
Let's see how much
she's "rocked" by all this.

15:16.568 --> 15:17.739
Tricia?

15:17.807 --> 15:20.981
Tom, I'm standing here
with Mayor Adam West,

15:21.049 --> 15:23.255
with the latest information
about the disappearance

15:23.324 --> 15:25.095
of young Scotty Jennings.

15:25.164 --> 15:27.035
What can you tell us,
Mr. Mayor?

15:27.102 --> 15:29.442
Please, Mr. Mayor
is my father.

15:29.510 --> 15:31.083
Call me John Mayor.

15:31.151 --> 15:33.591
Your body is a
wonderland, by the way.

15:33.658 --> 15:37.369
What is the city doing
to help rescue the missing boy?

15:37.437 --> 15:39.211
Well, we're looking
for this child

15:39.279 --> 15:42.789
using all the latest technology,
including the newest,

15:42.857 --> 15:45.329
most advanced
multimedia milk cartons.

15:45.398 --> 15:46.769
Help me!
I'm missing!

15:46.837 --> 15:48.007
Help!

15:48.074 --> 15:49.644
Why are you still
eating breakfast?!

15:49.711 --> 15:50.848
I'm kidnapped!

15:50.916 --> 15:52.689
Why are you turning me
the other way?!

15:52.757 --> 15:54.126
I'm still here!

15:54.194 --> 15:55.565
Scotty Jennings?

15:55.630 --> 15:57.152
Oh, my God!

15:57.220 --> 15:58.993
I know she was upset,
but do you think

15:59.060 --> 16:00.914
Lois would've gone
so far as to kidnap him?

16:00.982 --> 16:02.052
Of course she did.

16:02.119 --> 16:03.155
She'll do anything
for attention.

16:03.222 --> 16:04.359
I know.

16:04.427 --> 16:05.797
She's like the boy
who cried wolf.

16:05.864 --> 16:07.454
(sheep bleating)

16:07.522 --> 16:08.724
Wolf, wolf!

16:08.809 --> 16:10.094
Did you hear that?

16:10.163 --> 16:11.985
Somebody needs help!
Let's go!

16:14.359 --> 16:15.279
(screams)

16:15.347 --> 16:17.052
Oh, my God, Charles!

16:17.119 --> 16:18.925
Oh, my God,
I'll run and get help.

16:18.993 --> 16:20.464
No, no, we've got
to carry him!

16:20.532 --> 16:22.603
We can't leave him
here; there's a wolf!

16:22.672 --> 16:25.280
Um, there's not
really a wolf.

16:25.348 --> 16:26.417
What?!

16:26.485 --> 16:29.159
Tell my kids I love 'em.

16:29.228 --> 16:32.371
Charlie! Charlie!

16:32.438 --> 16:35.245
This was so funny in my head
when I planned it.

16:37.940 --> 16:39.276
Don't you worry, Scotty.

16:39.326 --> 16:40.998
We're gonna get you
to the hospital

16:41.067 --> 16:42.787
and get you the medical
attention you need.

16:42.839 --> 16:44.092
Yeah, hang in
there, buddy.

16:44.143 --> 16:46.099
When this is over, we
can get some ice cream.

16:46.150 --> 16:48.238
Me and Lois can get
some ice cream, not you.

16:48.305 --> 16:49.995
They're gonna be sticking
needles in you everywhere.

16:50.079 --> 16:51.315
You know, Peter,
you were right,

16:51.368 --> 16:53.006
this is actually
kind of a rush.

16:53.088 --> 16:55.430
I mean, look at us,
we're like Thelma and Louise.

16:55.497 --> 16:57.855
Yeah, but we all know that
didn't end well for them.

16:57.940 --> 16:59.142
(sirens wailing)

16:59.194 --> 17:00.530
You know what?

17:00.613 --> 17:02.989
Let's just turn ourselves in.

17:03.040 --> 17:04.742
I got a great lawyer.

17:04.828 --> 17:07.335
And he says, worst case,
eight to 12 years.

17:07.386 --> 17:09.058
And when we get out,
we'll still have

17:09.142 --> 17:10.730
the rest of our
lives ahead of us.

17:17.469 --> 17:19.210
(women screaming)

17:19.277 --> 17:20.246
(crash)

17:20.314 --> 17:22.084
Good-bye, terrible women.

17:28.707 --> 17:30.162
Oh, my God!

17:32.303 --> 17:34.259
This is Tricia Takanawa.

17:34.324 --> 17:37.067
I am standing outside
Quahog Hospital,

17:37.135 --> 17:39.676
where accused kidnappers
Lois and Peter Griffin

17:39.744 --> 17:41.148
have just arrived.

17:41.216 --> 17:44.091
Also arriving is
my overprotective boyfriend,

17:44.160 --> 17:47.436
who is suspicious whenever I am
called into work at night,

17:47.504 --> 17:50.577
even though I've been a
reporter for years, Tyrone.

17:50.645 --> 17:53.086
I thought I told you
to mention my painting business.

17:56.032 --> 17:58.371
Lois, Peter, stop right there.

17:58.439 --> 17:59.744
You're under arrest
for kidnapping.

17:59.812 --> 18:01.382
I'm gonna have to ask you

18:01.450 --> 18:03.052
to hand over the baby
and surrender.

18:03.120 --> 18:05.261
Joe, please get out of our way.

18:05.329 --> 18:08.005
I promise, when this is over,
I'll gladly go to prison

18:08.070 --> 18:10.513
for the rest of my life,
but not until I bring

18:10.579 --> 18:12.587
this defenseless child
into the hospital

18:12.654 --> 18:14.492
to get him the treatment
he deserves.

18:14.559 --> 18:17.200
Uh, Joe, we would
like two tickets

18:17.269 --> 18:18.303
to the
Policeman's Ball.

18:18.371 --> 18:19.273
Too late!

18:19.341 --> 18:20.278
(tires screech)

18:20.330 --> 18:21.416
There they are!

18:21.483 --> 18:23.824
Lois, please!

18:23.892 --> 18:26.398
Stop what you're doing and
give Scotty back to us!

18:26.466 --> 18:27.937
I can't do that, Hope.

18:28.005 --> 18:30.511
But we've entrusted our
son into the Lord's hands.

18:30.579 --> 18:31.881
I know.

18:31.950 --> 18:34.092
And maybe that's why
he ended up in my hands.

18:34.160 --> 18:36.666
The Lord can't do everything,
you know.

18:36.733 --> 18:37.971
Blasphemy!
Heresy!

18:38.037 --> 18:39.373
Sodomy!

18:39.442 --> 18:40.744
(chuckles) Sorry, I don't even
know what's going on.

18:40.812 --> 18:41.765
How you doin'?

18:41.833 --> 18:43.171
Ben, Hope,

18:43.238 --> 18:45.211
I know you don't believe
in modern medicine,

18:45.279 --> 18:47.552
but you do believe
in the power of prayer.

18:47.619 --> 18:48.454
That's right.

18:48.523 --> 18:49.827
And through the years,

18:49.894 --> 18:51.699
when there was disease
or infection,

18:51.765 --> 18:54.508
people of good faith
would pray to God for a cure.

18:54.576 --> 18:56.113
Yes. It's what we do.

18:56.181 --> 18:59.458
Well, then isn't it possible
that penicillin, vaccines

18:59.526 --> 19:02.703
and antibiotics are all
actually answered prayers?

19:04.209 --> 19:05.777
And isn't it possible that

19:05.845 --> 19:07.570
the amazing men and women
of medicine

19:07.637 --> 19:09.390
who brought about these miracles

19:09.458 --> 19:12.702
could be the instruments
of God's answers to our prayers?

19:12.770 --> 19:13.923
It's good so far, Lois.

19:13.974 --> 19:15.895
Try to work a few laughs
in there if you can.

19:15.964 --> 19:17.703
Look, I believe
life is sacred.

19:17.770 --> 19:20.110
And I know you want Scotty
to live a full life.

19:20.178 --> 19:21.314
(laughs)

19:21.382 --> 19:22.786
And if that's
true, then I think

19:22.855 --> 19:24.124
it's wrong for
you to ignore

19:24.192 --> 19:26.264
what very well could
be the Lord's will.

19:26.331 --> 19:28.437
I mean, what's the
point in praying to God

19:28.506 --> 19:30.777
if you're just going to wipe
your butt with his answers?

19:32.436 --> 19:34.958
Hope, Ben,

19:35.026 --> 19:37.367
please let God
answer your prayers.

19:37.418 --> 19:39.272
Please let your son get help.

19:40.779 --> 19:42.953
Well, I guess through
the Lord's will,

19:43.019 --> 19:45.694
anything is possible.

19:45.761 --> 19:46.965
All right, Lois.

19:47.033 --> 19:48.571
Scotty can have
his treatment.

19:48.639 --> 19:50.243
Oh, thank you!

19:50.294 --> 19:52.903
Thank you,
and God bless you both!

19:52.969 --> 19:54.157
Hey, everybody!

19:54.223 --> 19:55.760
We're all gonna get laid!

19:55.828 --> 19:58.839
(wild cheering)

20:03.286 --> 20:06.196
<i>TV ANNOUNCER: We now return to
Dracula in San Francisco.</i>

20:19.273 --> 20:20.508
Ooh.

20:20.576 --> 20:23.018
Well, that's why
we have the lab.

20:23.085 --> 20:25.041
Well, I just got off
the phone with Hope,

20:25.126 --> 20:27.651
and it sounds like Scotty's
gonna make a full recovery.

20:27.719 --> 20:29.123
You hear that, Stewie?

20:29.189 --> 20:30.728
Looks like your little
friend's gonna be okay.

20:30.795 --> 20:32.166
Eh, I don't care about him.

20:32.233 --> 20:33.839
I've got a new friend
who's got leprosy.

20:35.279 --> 20:36.848
(chuckles)
See, he's funny.

20:36.916 --> 20:38.922
Peter, are you actually reading
that Christian Science book?

20:38.989 --> 20:41.095
Yeah, you know, I figured
I'd give it a shot.

20:41.163 --> 20:43.067
I mean, wouldn't it
be cool if you could

20:43.136 --> 20:45.793
pray really hard for something,
and it actually happened?

20:48.404 --> 20:50.711
I am so happy for me.

20:50.779 --> 20:52.249
I deserve this.

20:52.300 --> 20:53.804
When do you think
the Queen's gonna die?

20:53.805 --> 21:54.805
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru